# Caddy config for Protocol Lab #11.
#
# The site is named (www.example.lab) rather than a bare `:443` so Caddy's
# internal CA has a subject to issue a leaf certificate for; a bare `:443`
# site has no hostname, so `tls internal` produces no servable cert and every
# handshake fails with an internal-error alert. The host part only controls
# SNI/Host *matching* — Caddy still binds the wildcard `:443` on all
# interfaces, so this does not depend on the lab IP being assigned first.
# The client reaches it with `curl --resolve www.example.lab:443:10.0.0.2`.
#
# `tls internal` uses Caddy's own CA (no public CA, no Internet). The response
# body echoes the protocol that served the request, so a fetch over HTTP/2 vs
# HTTP/3 is self-labeling.
{
	auto_https disable_redirects
	local_certs
}

www.example.lab:443 {
	tls internal
	respond "Hello over {http.request.proto} for {http.request.uri.path}\n" 200
}
